    "result_text": "The full suite is green (the project's surefire config runs the acceptance suite, which is the relevant test set).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `membershipNumber` formatted `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year.\n\n**Changes (2 files):**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` expression to `toOwnerDto`, computing the value the same way as the existing `displayName`/`initials` derivations:\n   ```java\n   owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100)\n   ```\n\n**Structural impact kept low:** the derivation lives in the small `OwnerMapper` interface (low `WMC_other`) rather than the large `Owner` entity class, matching the existing pattern for computed fields. `toOwnerDto` has CC 1, and I added a single cohesive mapping line \u2014 no method or class was grown.\n\nThe `%02d` format guarantees a two-digit year (e.g. `SMI-0007-M07` for 2007, `SMI-0007-M26` for 2026), matching the test's `registrationDate.substring(2,4)` expectation.",
